  "durationSeconds": 32.125,
  "caption": "Day 191 of How to Not Be a Psychopath\n\nBeing good at being alone doesn’t mean you stop wanting love, touch, connection, or companionship.\n\nIt means loneliness stops making your decisions for you.\n\nYou stop treating attention like proof that you matter. You stop letting someone’s interest become more important than your own peace. And you stop confusing being chosen with being valuable.\n\nThe goal isn’t to need nobody.\n\nIt’s to know your worth before somebody else decides they want you.",
  "transcript": {
    "text": "If being alone makes you question your worth, you're probably not afraid of solitude. You're afraid that if nobody is choosing you, then maybe you aren't worth choosing. That's why almost anybody can start to feel like relief. The goal isn't to stop needing people. The goal is to stop abandoning yourself the second somebody wants you. If nobody's told you this today, I love you. I believe in you. If you want to do hard things, you can do hard things. You got this. Come back tomorrow so we can all be a little less crazy together. I love you, y'all. Peace.",
